STORY.scripture({"1 KĔPHA 2:24":{"t":"who Himself bore our sins in His body on the timber, so that we, having died to sins, might live unto righteousness – by whose stripes you were healed.","book":"1 KĔPHA"},"DANI'AL 2:44":{"t":"“And in the days of these sovereigns the Al of the shamayim shall set up a reign which shall never be destroyed, nor the reign pass on to other people – it crushes and puts to an end all these reigns and it shall stand forever.","book":"DANI'AL"},"DANI'AL 8:21":{"t":"“And the male goat is the sovereign of Greece and the large horn between its eyes is the first sovereign.","book":"DANI'AL"},"EZRA 1:1":{"t":"And in the first year of Koresh sovereign of Persia, that the Word of (YAHUAH) HWHY by the mouth of Yahrmeyah might be accomplished, (YAHUAH) HWHY stirred up the ruach of Koresh sovereign of Persia, to proclaim throughout all his reign and also in writing, saying,","book":"EZRA"},"GALATIANS 4:4":{"t":"But when the completion of the time came, Aluahim sent forth His Son, born of a woman, born under Torah,","book":"GALATIANS"},"LUKE 1:26":{"t":"And in the sixth month the mal'ak Gaḇri’al was sent by Aluahim to a city of Galil named Natsareth,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:27":{"t":"to a maiden engaged to a man whose name was Yosĕph, of the house of Dawiḏ. And the maiden’s name was Miryam.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:28":{"t":"And the mal'ak, coming to her, said, “Greetings, favoured one, the Master is with you. Baruk are you among women!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:29":{"t":"But she was greatly disturbed at his word and wondered what kind of greeting this was.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:30-33":{"t":"And the mal'ak said to her, “Do not be afraid, Miryam, for you have found chen with Aluahim. “And see, you shall conceive in your womb and shall give birth to a Son and call His Name Yahusha. ”He shall be great and shall be called the Son of the Most High. And (YAHUAH) HWHY Aluahim shall give Him the throne of His father Dawiḏ. “And He shall reign over the house of Ya‛aqoḇ forever and there shall be no end to His reign.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:34":{"t":"And Miryam said to the mal'ak, “How shall this be, since I do not know a man?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:35-37":{"t":"And the mal'ak answering, said to her, “The Ruach HaQadash shall come upon you and the power of the Most High shall overshadow you. And for that reason the Qadash (Set Apart One) born of you shall be called: Son of Aluahim. “And see, Alisheḇa your relative, she has also conceived a son in her old age. And this is now the sixth month to her who was called barren, because with Aluahim no matter shall be impossible.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:38":{"t":"And Miryam said, “See the female servant of (YAHUAH) HWHY! Let it be to me according to your word.” And the mal'ak went away from her.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:1":{"t":"And it came to be in those days that a decree went out from Caesar Augustus for all the world to be registered.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:10":{"t":"And the mal'ak said to them, “Do not be afraid, for look, I bring you the besorah of great joy which shall be to all people.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:11":{"t":"“Because there was born to you today in the city of Dawiḏ a Saviour, who is Mashiach, the Master.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:12":{"t":"“And this is the sign to you: You shall find a baby wrapped up, lying in a feeding trough.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:13":{"t":"And suddenly there was with the mal'ak a crowd of the heavenly host praising Aluahim and saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:14":{"t":"“Esteem to Aluahim in the highest and on earth shalom among men with whom He is pleased!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:15":{"t":"It came to be, when the mal'akim had gone away from them into the shamayim, that the shepherds said to each other, “Indeed, let us go to Bĕyth Leḥem and see this matter that has taken place, which the Master has made known to us.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:16":{"t":"And they came in haste and found Miryam and Yosĕph and the baby lying in a feeding trough.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:17":{"t":"And having seen, they made known the matter which was spoken to them concerning the child.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:18":{"t":"And all those who heard marvelled at what the shepherds said to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:19":{"t":"But Miryam kept all these matters, considering them in her heart.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:2-3":{"t":"This took place as a first registration while Quirinius was governing Syria. And all were going to be registered, each one to his own city.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:20":{"t":"And the shepherds returned, boasting and praising Aluahim for all they had heard and seen, as it was spoken to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:4-5":{"t":"And Yosĕph also went up from Galil, out of the city of Natsareth to Yahuḏah, to the city of Dawiḏ, which is called Bĕyth Leḥem, because he was of the house and lineage of Dawiḏ, to be registered with Miryam, who was engaged to him – being pregnant.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:7":{"t":"And she gave birth to her first-born Son and wrapped Him up and laid Him down in a feeding trough, because there was no room for them in a lodging place.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:8":{"t":"And in the same country there were shepherds living out in the fields, keeping watch over their flock by night.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:9":{"t":"And look, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY stood before them and the esteem of (YAHUAH) HWHY shone around them and they were greatly afraid.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:1-2":{"t":"And in the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, when Pontius Pilate was governor of Yahuḏah and Herodes district ruler of Galil and his brother Philip district ruler of Yahtur and the country of Trachonitis and Lusanias district ruler of Aḇilene, Ḥanan and Qayapha being kohen gadols, the Word of Aluahim came to Yahuchanon the son of Zaḵaryahu in the wilderness.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:10":{"t":"And the crowds asked him, saying, “What, then, shall we do?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:11":{"t":"And answering He said to them, “Let him who has two undergarments share with him who has none and let him who has food do likewise.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:12":{"t":"And tax collectors also came to be immersed and said to him, “Teacher, what shall we do?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:13":{"t":"And he said to them, “Collect no more than what is appointed for you.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:14":{"t":"And soldiers also asked him, saying, “What shall we do?” And he said to them, “Do not intimidate anyone or accuse falsely and be satisfied with your pay.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:15":{"t":"But as the people were in expectation and all were reasoning in their hearts about Yahuchanon,whether he was the Mashiach or not,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:16-17":{"t":"Yahuchanon answered, saying to them all, “I indeed immerse you in water, but One mightier than I is coming, whose sandal straps I am not worthy to loosen. He shall immerse you in the Ruach HaQadash and fire. “His winnowing fork is in His hand and He shall thoroughly cleanse His threshing-floor and gather the wheat into His storehouse, but the chaff He shall burn with unquenchable fire.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:18":{"t":"And urging with many other words, he brought the besorah to the people.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:14-15":{"t":"And Yahusha returned in the power of the Ruach to Galil and news of Him went out through all the surrounding country. And He was teaching in their qahalim, being praised by all.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:16":{"t":"And He came to Natsareth, where He had been brought up. And according to His practice, He went into the qahal on the Shabbath day and stood up to read.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:17":{"t":"And the scroll of the naḇi Yahshayahu was handed to Him. And having unrolled the scroll, He found the place where it was written:","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:18-19":{"t":"“The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because He has anointed Me to bring the Besorah to the poor. He has sent Me to heal the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to send away crushed ones with a release, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:18-21":{"t":"“The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because He has anointed Me to bring the Besorah to the poor. He has sent Me to heal the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to send away crushed ones with a release, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY.” And having rolled up the scroll, He gave it back to the attendant and sat down. And the eyes of all in the qahal were fixed upon Him. And He began to say to them, “Today this Scripture has been filled in your hearing.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:20":{"t":"And having rolled up the scroll, He gave it back to the attendant and sat down. And the eyes of all in the qahal were fixed upon Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:21":{"t":"And He began to say to them, “Today this Scripture has been filled in your hearing.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:22":{"t":"And all were bearing witness to Him and marvelled at the pleasant words that came out of His mouth. And they said, “Is this not the son of Yosĕph?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:23":{"t":"And He said to them, “No doubt, you shall say this proverb to Me, ‘Physician, heal yourself! Whatever we have heard being done in Kephar Naḥum, do also here in Your country.’ ”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:24":{"t":"And He said, “Truly, I say to you, no naḇi is accepted in his own country.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:25-26":{"t":"“But truly I say to you, many widows were in Yasharal in the days of Aliyahu, when the shamayim was shut up for three years and six months and there was a great scarcity of food in all the land, and Aliyahu was sent to none of them, but to Tsarephath of Tsiḏon, to a woman, a widow.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:27":{"t":"“And many lepers were in Yasharal in the time of Alisha the naḇi and none of them was cleansed except Na‛aman the Aramean.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:28-29":{"t":"And all those in the qahal, when they heard this, were filled with wrath. And rising up they drove Him out of the city and brought Him to the brow of the hill on which their city was built, in order to throw Him down.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:30":{"t":"But He, passing through the midst of them, went away.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:1":{"t":"And it came to be, while the crowd was pressing upon Him to hear the word of Aluahim, that He stood by the Lake of Gennĕsar,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:10":{"t":"so too were Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon, the sons of Zaḇdai, who were partners with Shim‛on. Then Yahusha said to Shim‛on, “Do not fear, from now on you shall catch men.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:11":{"t":"And having brought the boats to land, they left all and followed Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:2":{"t":"and He saw two boats standing by the lake, but the fishermen had gone from them and were washing their nets.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:3":{"t":"And entering into one of the boats, which belonged to Shim‛on, He asked him to pull away a little from the land. And He sat down and was teaching the crowds from the boat.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:4":{"t":"And when He ceased speaking, He said to Shim‛on, “Pull out into the deep and let down your nets for a catch.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:5":{"t":"And Shim‛on answering, said to Him, “Master, we have toiled all night and caught none but at Your word I shall let down the net.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:6-7":{"t":"And when they did so, they caught a great number of fish and their net was breaking, and they motioned to their partners in the other boat to come and help them. And they came and filled both the boats, so that they were sinking.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:8":{"t":"And when Shim‛on Kĕpha saw it, he fell down at the knees of Yahusha, saying, “Depart from me, for I am a man, a sinner, O Master!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:9":{"t":"For astonishment had seized him and all those with him, at the catch of fish which they took,","book":"LUKE"},"MARK 1:12":{"t":"And immediately the Ruach drove Him into the wilderness.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:21":{"t":"And they went into Kephar Naḥum and immediately on the Shabbath He went into the qahal and taught.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:22":{"t":"And they were astonished at His teaching, for He was teaching them as possessing authority and not as the scribes.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:23-24":{"t":"And there was a man in their qahal with an unclean ruach and he cried out, saying, “Ha! What have we to do with You, Yahusha of Natsareth? Did You come to destroy us? I know who You are: the Qadash (Set Apart One) of Aluahim!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:25":{"t":"And Yahusha rebuked him, saying, “Be silenced and come out of Him!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:26":{"t":"And throwing him into convulsions, the unclean ruach called out with a loud voice and came out of him.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:27":{"t":"And they were all so amazed, as to reason among themselves, saying, “What is this, a fresh teaching? With authority He commands even the unclean ruchot and they obey Him!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:28":{"t":"And news about Him immediately spread into all the country around Galil.","book":"MARK"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:2-3":{"t":"And when Yahuchanon had heard in the prison of the works of Mashiach, he sent two of his taught ones and said to Him, “Are You the Coming One or do we look for another?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:4-6":{"t":"And Yahusha answering, said to them, “Go, report to Yahuchanon what you hear and see: “Blind receive sight and lame walk, lepers are cleansed and deaf hear, dead are raised up and poor are brought the Besorah. “Baruk is he who does not stumble in Me.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:5":{"t":"“Blind receive sight and lame walk, lepers are cleansed and deaf hear, dead are raised up and poor are brought the Besorah.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:22-23":{"t":"And immediately Yahusha made His taught ones enter into the boat and go before Him to the other side, while He dismissed the crowds. And having dismissed the crowds, He went up to the mountain by Himself to pray. And when evening had come, He was alone there.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:24":{"t":"But the boat was now in the middle of the sea, agitated by the waves, for the ruach was against it.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:25":{"t":"And in the fourth watch of the night Yahusha went to them, walking on the sea.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:26":{"t":"And when the taught ones saw Him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, “It is a phantom!” And from fear they cried.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:27":{"t":"But immediately Yahusha spoke to them, saying, “Take courage, it is I, do not be afraid.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:28":{"t":"And Kĕpha answered Him and said, “Master, if it is You, command me to come to You on the water.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:29":{"t":"And He said, “Come.” And when Kĕpha had come down out of the boat, he walked on the water to go to Yahusha.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:30":{"t":"But when he saw that the ruach was strong, he was afraid. And beginning to sink, he cried out, saying, “Master, save me!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:31":{"t":"And immediately Yahusha stretched out His hand and took hold of him and said to him, “O you of little belief, why did you doubt?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:32":{"t":"And when they came into the boat, the ruach ceased.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:33":{"t":"And those in the boat came and did bow to Him, saying, “Truly You are the Son of Aluahim.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:18":{"t":"But the birth of Yahusha Mashiach was as follows: After His mother Miryam was engaged to Yosĕph, before they came together, she was found to be pregnant from the Ruach HaQadash.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:19":{"t":"And Yosĕph her husband, being righteous and not wishing to make a show of her, had in mind to put her away secretly.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:20-21":{"t":"But while he thought about this, see, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to him in a dream, saying, “Yosĕph, son of Dawiḏ, do not be afraid to take Miryam as your wife, for that which is in her was brought forth from the Ruach HaQadash. “She shall give birth to a Son and you shall call His Name Yahusha for He shall save His people from their sins. ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:22-23":{"t":"And all this came to be in order to fill what was spoken by (YAHUAH) HWHY through the naḇi, saying, “See, a maiden shall conceive and she shall give birth to a Son and they shall call His Name Immanu’al,” which translated, means, “Al with us.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:24":{"t":"And Yosĕph, awaking from his sleep, did as the mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY commanded him and took his wife,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:1":{"t":"And Yahusha having been born in Bĕyth Leḥem of Yahuḏah in the days of Herodes the sovereign, see, Magi from the East came to Yahrushalayim,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:10":{"t":"And seeing the star, they rejoiced with exceedingly great joy.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:11":{"t":"And coming into the house, they saw the Child with Miryam His mother and fell down and did reverence to Him and opening their treasures, they presented to Him gifts of gold and frankincense and myrrh.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:12":{"t":"And having been warned in a dream that they should not return to Herodes, they departed for their own country by another way.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:13":{"t":"And when they had left, see, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to Yosĕph in a dream, saying, “Arise, take the Child and His mother and flee to Mitsrayim and remain there until I bring you word, for Herodes is about to seek the Child to destroy Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:14-15":{"t":"And rising up, he took the Child and His mother by night and departed for Mitsrayim, and remained there until the death of Herodes, to fill what was spoken by (YAHUAH) HWHY through the naḇi, saying, “Out of Mitsrayim I have called My Son.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:2":{"t":"saying, “Where is He who has been born Sovereign of the Yahuḏim? For we saw His star in the East and have come to do reverence to Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:3-4":{"t":"And Herodes the sovereign, having heard, was troubled and all Yahrushalayim with him. And having gathered all the chief kohanim and scribes of the people together, he asked them where the Mashiach was to be born.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:5-6":{"t":"And they said to him, “In Bĕyth Leḥem of Yahuḏah, for thus it has been written by the naḇi, ‘But you, Bĕyth Leḥem, in the land of Yahuḏah, you are by no means least among the rulers of Yahuḏah, for out of you shall come a Ruler who shall shepherd My people Yasharal.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:7":{"t":"Then Herodes, having called the Magi secretly, learned exactly from them what time the star appeared.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:8":{"t":"And having sent them to Bĕyth Leḥem, he said, “Go and search diligently for the Child and when you have found Him, bring back word to me, so that I too might go and do reverence to Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:9":{"t":"And having heard the sovereign, they went. And see, the star which they had seen in the East went before them, until it came and stood over where the Child was.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:1":{"t":"And in those days Yahuchanon the Immerser came proclaiming in the wilderness of Yahuḏah,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:13":{"t":"Then Yahusha came from Galil to Yahuchanon at the Yardĕn to be immersed by him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:14":{"t":"But Yahuchanon was hindering Him, saying, “I need to be immersed by You and You come to me?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:15":{"t":"But Yahusha answering, said to him, “Permit it now, for thus it is fitting for us to fill all righteousness.” Then he permitted Him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:16":{"t":"And having been immersed, Yahusha went up immediately from the water and see, the shamayim were opened and He saw the Ruach of Aluahim descending like a dove and coming upon Him,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:17":{"t":"and see, a voice out of the shamayim, saying, “This is My Son, the Beloved, in whom I did delight.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:2":{"t":"and saying, “Repent, for the reign of the shamayim has come near!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:3":{"t":"For this is he who was spoken of by the naḇi Yahshayahu, saying, “A voice of one crying in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY, make His paths straight.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:4":{"t":"And Yahuchanon had a garment of camel’s hair and a leather girdle around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:5-6":{"t":"Then Yahrushalayim and all Yahuḏah and all the country around the Yardĕn went out to him, and they were immersed by him in the Yardĕn, confessing their sins.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:1":{"t":"Then Yahusha was led up by the Ruach into the wilderness to be tried by the devil.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:10":{"t":"Then Yahusha said to him, “Go, Satan! For it has been written, ‘You shall worship (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim and Him alone you shall serve.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:11":{"t":"Then the devil left Him and see, mal'akim came and attended Him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:2":{"t":"And after having fasted forty days and forty nights, He was hungry.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:3":{"t":"And the trier came and said to Him, “If You are the Son of Aluahim, command that these stones become bread.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:4":{"t":"But He answering, said, “It has been written, ‘Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes from the mouth of (YAHUAH) HWHY.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:5":{"t":"Then the devil took Him up into the qadash (Set Apart) city, set Him on the edge of the Qodash (Set Apart Place),","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:6":{"t":"and said to Him, “If You are the Son of Aluahim, throw Yourself down. For it has been written, ‘He shall command His mal'akim concerning you,’ and ‘In their hands they shall bear you up so that you do not dash your foot against a stone.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:7":{"t":"Yahusha said to him, “It has also been written, ‘You shall not try (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:8":{"t":"Again, the devil took Him up on a very high mountain and showed Him all the reigns of the world and their esteem,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:9":{"t":"and said to Him, “All these I shall give You if You fall down and worship me.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:1-2":{"t":"But when He saw the crowds, He went up on a mountain and when He was seated His taught ones came to Him. And having opened His mouth, He was teaching them, saying,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:11-12":{"t":"“Baruk are you when they reproach and persecute you and falsely say every wicked word against you, for My sake. “Rejoice and be glad, because your reward in the shamayim is great. For in this way they persecuted the naḇi'im who were before you.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:3-6":{"t":"“Baruk are the poor in ruach, because theirs is the reign of the shamayim. “Baruk are those who mourn, because they shall be comforted. “Baruk are the meek, because they shall inherit the earth. “Baruk are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, because they shall be filled.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:7-10":{"t":"“Baruk are the compassionate, because they shall obtain compassion. “Baruk are the clean in heart, because they shall see Aluahim. “Baruk are the peacemakers, because they shall be called sons of Aluahim. “Baruk are those persecuted for righteousness’ sake, because theirs is the reign of the shamayim.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 7:28-29":{"t":"And it came to be, when Yahusha had ended these words, that the people were astonished at His teaching, for He was teaching them as one possessing authority and not as the scribes.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:10":{"t":"And when Yahusha heard, He marvelled and said to those who followed, “Truly, I say to you, not even in Yasharal have I found such great belief!","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:11-12":{"t":"“And I say to you that many shall come from east and west and sit down with Aḇrahim and Yahtsḥaq and Ya‛aqoḇ in the reign of the shamayim, but the sons of the reign shall be cast out into outer darkness – there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:13":{"t":"And Yahusha said to the captain, “Go and as you have believed, so let it be done for you.” And his servant was healed that hour.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:5-6":{"t":"And when Yahusha had entered Kephar Naḥum, a captain came to Him, appealing to Him, saying, “Master, my servant is lying in the house paralysed, grievously tortured.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:7":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “I shall come and heal him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:8":{"t":"And the captain answering, said, “Master, I am not worthy that You should come under my roof. But only say a word and my servant shall be healed.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:9":{"t":"“For I too am a man under authority, having soldiers under me. And I say to this one, ‘Go,’ and he goes and to another, ‘Come,’ and he comes and to my servant, ‘Do this,’ and he does it.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:27":{"t":"And as Yahusha passed on from there, two blind men followed Him, crying out and saying, “Son of Dawiḏ, have compassion on us!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:28":{"t":"And when He came into the house, the blind men came to Him. And Yahusha said to them, “Do you believe that I am able to do this?” They said to Him, “Yea, Master.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:29":{"t":"Then He touched their eyes, saying, “According to your belief let it be to you.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:30":{"t":"And their eyes were opened. And Yahusha strictly ordered them, saying, “See, let no one know.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:31":{"t":"But when they went out, they made Him known in all that land.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"YAHUCHANON 1:19":{"t":"Now this was the witness of Yahuchanon when the Yahuḏim sent from Yahrushalayim kohanim and Lĕwites to ask him, “Who are you?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:20":{"t":"And he confessed and did not deny, but confessed, “I am not the Mashiach.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:21":{"t":"And they asked him, “What then, are you Aliyahu?” So he said, “I am not.” “Are you the Naḇi?” And he answered, “No.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:22":{"t":"Therefore they said to him, “Who are you, so that we give an answer to those who sent us? What do you say about yourself?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:23":{"t":"He said, “I am a voice of one crying in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY,’ as the naḇi Yahshayahu said.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:24":{"t":"And those sent were of the Pharisees,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:25":{"t":"and they asked him, saying,“Why then do you immerse if you are not the Mashiach, nor Aliyahu, nor the Naḇi?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:26-27":{"t":"Yahuchanon answered them, saying, “I immerse in water, but in your midst stands One whom you do not know, the One coming after me, who has become before me, whose sandal strap I am not worthy to loosen.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:28":{"t":"This took place in Bĕyth Anyah beyond the Yardĕn, where Yahuchanon was immersing.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:29":{"t":"The next day Yahuchanon saw Yahusha coming toward him, and said, “See, the Lamb of Aluahim who takes away the sin of the world!","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:30-31":{"t":"“This is He of whom I said,‘After me comes a Man who has become before me, for He was before me.’ “And I did not know Him, but that He might be revealed to Yasharal, therefore I came immersing in water.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:32-34":{"t":"And Yahuchanon bore witness, saying, “I have seen the Ruach coming down from shamayim like a dove and remain on Him. “And I did not know Him, but He who sent me to immerse in water said to me, ‘Upon whom you see the Ruach coming down and remaining on Him, this is He who immerses in the Ruach HaQadash.’ “And I have seen and have witnessed that this is the Son of Aluahim.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:35":{"t":"Again the following day, Yahuchanon was standing with two of his taught ones,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:36":{"t":"and looking at Yahusha walking, he said, “See the Lamb of Aluahim!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:37":{"t":"And the two taught ones heard him speaking and they followed Yahusha.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:38":{"t":"And Yahusha turning, and seeing them following, said to them, “What do you seek?” And they said to Him, “Rabbi” (which means Teacher), “where are You staying?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:39":{"t":"He said to them, “Come and see.” They went and saw where He was staying, and remained with Him that day. Now it was about the tenth hour.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:40":{"t":"Andri, the brother of Shim‛on Kĕpha, was one of the two who heard from Yahuchanon, and followed Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:41":{"t":"First he found his own brother Shim‛on and said to him, “We have found the Mashiach” (which means the Anointed).","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:42":{"t":"And he brought him to Yahusha. And looking at him, Yahusha said,“You are Shim‛on, the son of Yonah, you shall be called Kĕpha” (which means A Stone).","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:1":{"t":"And on the third day there was a wedding in Qanah of Galil, and the mother of Yahusha was there.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:10":{"t":"and said to him, “Every man at the beginning sets out the good wine and, when they have drunk, then that which is poorer. You have kept the good wine until now.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:11":{"t":"This, the beginning of the signs, Yahusha did in Qanah of Galil, and manifested His esteem. And His taught ones believed in Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:2":{"t":"And both Yahusha and His taught ones were invited to the wedding.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:3":{"t":"And when they were short of wine, the mother of Yahusha said to Him, “They have no wine.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:4":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “Woman, what is that to Me and to you? My hour has not yet come.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:5":{"t":"His mother said to the servants, “Do whatever He says to you.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:6":{"t":"And there were six stone water-jugs standing there, according to the mode of cleansing of the Yahuḏim, each holding two or three measures.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:7":{"t":"Yahusha said to them, “Fill the water-jugs with water.” And they filled them up to the brim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:8":{"t":"And He said to them,“Now draw out and take it to the master of the feast.” So they took it.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:9":{"t":"But when the master of the feast had tasted the water that had become wine, and did not know where it came from – though the servants who had drawn the water knew – the master of the feast called the bridegroom,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:1-2":{"t":"After this Yahusha went away to the other side of the Sea of Galil, that is Lake Kinnereth. And a large crowd was following Him, because they saw His signs which He did on those who were sick.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:10":{"t":"And Yahusha said, “Make the people sit down.” Now there was much grass in the place, and the men, numbering about five thousand, sat down.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:11":{"t":"And Yahusha took the loaves and having given thanks He distributed them to the taught ones and the taught ones to those sitting down. And the same with the fish, as much as they wished.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:12":{"t":"And when they were filled, He said to His taught ones, “Gather the broken pieces that are left over, so that none gets wasted.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:13":{"t":"So they gathered them and filled twelve baskets with broken pieces of the five barley loaves which were left over by those who had eaten.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:14":{"t":"Then the men, having seen the sign that Yahusha did, said, “This is truly the Naḇi who is coming to the world.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:3-4":{"t":"And Yahusha went up on a mountain, and there He sat down with His taught ones. And the Pesach was near, the festival of the Yahuḏim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:5":{"t":"Then Yahusha, lifting up His eyes and seeing a large crowd coming toward Him, said to Philip, “Where shall we buy bread for them to eat?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:6":{"t":"And this He said, trying him, for He Himself knew what He would do.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:7":{"t":"Philip answered Him, “Two hundred pieces of silver worth of bread is not sufficient for them, for every one of them to receive a little.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:8-9":{"t":"One of His taught ones, Andri, the brother of Shim‛on Kĕpha, said to Him, “Here is a boy who has five barley loaves and two fish, but what are these for so many?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YASHAYAHU 11:1-2":{"t":"And a Rod shall come forth from the stump of Yahshai and a Sprout from his roots shall bear fruit. The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY shall rest upon Him – the Ruach of wisdom and understanding, the Ruach of counsel and might, the Ruach of knowledge and of the fear of (YAHUAH) HWHY,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 1:1":{"t":"The vision of Yahshayahu son of Amots, which he saw concerning Yahuḏah and Yahrushalayim in the days of Uzziyahu, Yotham, Aḥaz, Ḥizqiyahu – sovereigns of Yahuḏah.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 35:5-6":{"t":"Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened and the ears of the deaf be opened. Then the lame shall leap like a deer and the tongue of the dumb sing, because waters shall burst forth in the wilderness and streams in the desert.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 40:3":{"t":"The voice of one crying in the wilderness, “Prepare the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY; make straight in the desert a highway for our Aluahim.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 53:3-5":{"t":"despised and rejected by men, a man of pains and knowing sickness. And as one from whom the face is hidden, being despised and we did not consider Him. Truly, He has borne our sicknesses and carried our pains. Yet we reckoned Him stricken, smitten by Aluahim and afflicted. But He was pierced for our transgressions, He was crushed for our crookednesses. The chastisement for our shalom was upon Him and by His stripes we are healed.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 61:1-2":{"t":"The Ruach of the Master (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because (YAHUAH) HWHY has anointed Me to bring the besorah to the meek. He has sent Me to bind up the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and the opening of the prison to those who are bound, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY and the day of vengeance of our Aluahim, to comfort all who mourn,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:1":{"t":"In the year that Sovereign Uzziyahu died, I saw (YAHUAH) HWHY sitting on a throne, high and lifted up and the train of His robe filled the Hĕḵal.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:1":{"t":"And it came to be in the days of Aḥaz son of Yotham, son of Uzziyahu, sovereign of Yahuḏah, that Retsin sovereign of Aram and Peqaḥ son of Remalyahu, sovereign of Yasharal, went up to Yahrushalayim to fight against it, but could not prevail against it.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:10":{"t":"And (YAHUAH) HWHY spoke again to Aḥaz, saying,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:11":{"t":"“Ask a sign for yourself from (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim; make deep the request or make it high.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:12":{"t":"But Aḥaz said, “I do not ask nor try (YAHUAH) HWHY!”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:13":{"t":"And he said, “Hear now, O house of Dawiḏ! Is it not enough that you weary men, that you weary my Aluahim also?","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:14":{"t":"“Therefore (YAHUAH) HWHY Himself gives you a sign: Look, the maiden conceives and gives birth to a Son and shall call His Name Immanu’al.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:2":{"t":"And it was reported to the house of Dawiḏ, saying, “Aram has set up camp in Ephrayim.” And his heart and the heart of his people were moved as the trees of the forest are moved with the ruach.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:3":{"t":"And (YAHUAH) HWHY said to Yahshayahu, “Go out now to meet Aḥaz, you and She’ar-Yashuḇ your son, at the end of the channel of the upper pool, on the highway of the Launderer’s Field,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:4":{"t":"and say to him, ‘Take heed and be calm; do not fear or be faint-hearted for these two stubs of smoking fire brands, for the fierce displeasure of Retsin and Aram and the son of Remalyahu.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 8:16":{"t":"Bind up the witness and seal the Torah among my taught ones.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 8:17":{"t":"And I shall wait on (YAHUAH) HWHY, who hides His face from the house of Ya‛aqoḇ. And I shall look for Him.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 9:6-7":{"t":"For a Child shall be born unto us, a Son shall be given unto us and the rule is on His shoulder. And His Name is called Wonder, Counsellor, Strong Al, Father of Continuity, Prince of Shalom. Of the increase of His rule and shalom there is no end, upon the throne of Dawiḏ and over His reign, to establish it and sustain it with right-ruling and with righteousness from now on, even forever. The ardour of (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts does this.","book":"YASHAYAHU"}});
